"description" = "Secure your accounts with Autheris — a privacy-first two-factor authentication app for iPhone, iPad and Mac.\n\nAutheris generates the time-based one-time passwords (TOTP) that protect your most important accounts, and keeps the secrets behind them on your device. No account, no sign-up, no ads.\n\nKEY FEATURES\n• One-Tap Codes — Copy a code with a single tap. The clipboard clears itself after 60 seconds.\n• Pin and Reorder — Pin the codes you use most to the top, and drag the rest into whatever order suits you.\n• Recently Deleted — Delete a code by mistake? It stays on your device for 7 days, ready to restore.\n• QR Scanning — Add an account by scanning a QR code, or choose a screenshot from your photo library.\n• SHA-1, SHA-256 and SHA-512 — Including the services that need more than the default. If a service rejects your codes, the algorithm is editable per account.\n• Import — Bring your accounts across from Google Authenticator, Aegis, andOTP or 2FAS.\n• Search — Find any account instantly, however long your list gets.\n• Issuer Icons — Familiar brand marks so you can spot an account at a glance.\n• Countdown Ring — A clear, color-customizable ring shows how long each code has left.\n\nPRIVACY AND SECURITY\n• Face ID / Touch ID Lock — Locks when opened, and again after 30 seconds away.\n• Blurred When Backgrounded — Content blurs when you switch apps, and your codes are hidden in the app switcher.\n• Protected While Recording — Codes are covered whenever your screen is being recorded or mirrored.\n• Secrets Stay on Your Device — Codes and setup keys are kept in your device's Keychain and never leave your device unless you export them or turn on iCloud Sync.\n• Encrypted Backups — Save an AES-256-GCM encrypted backup protected by a password only you know.\n• Optional iCloud Sync — Off by default. When you enable it, your secrets are end-to-end encrypted by CloudKit, and the developer cannot read them.\n• No Account, No Tracking — Nothing to sign up for, no analytics, no advertising. Autheris is open source.\n\nInstall Autheris, add an account, and keep your second factor under your own control.";
"keywords" = "two-factor,mfa,2-factor,token,generator,security,privacy,private,backup,sync,icloud,vault";
"whatsNew" = "Autheris 2.3 adds a way to rate the app, and gives the Mac app its proper name.\n\n• You can now rate Autheris from Settings › Help, and the app will ask by itself once — after you change a setting, never on launch, and at most once per version.\n\n• On the Mac, the app is now called Autheris everywhere. It previously installed as Vaultic, so the Dock, the menu bar and your Applications folder called it something else — they now match the name the app already uses in the App Store.\n\n• Your codes, iCloud sync and settings are exactly where you left them.\n\n• If an older copy named Vaultic is still in your Applications folder, you can move it to the Trash — Autheris is the app from here on.";
"promotionalText" = "The Mac app is now named Autheris everywhere. No account, no tracking — your codes stay on your device.";
"marketingUrl" = "https://autheris.app";
"supportUrl" = "https://autheris.app";
